  "summary_md": "Today’s furnishings batch splits between names managing housing-linked headwinds and a cluster executing dramatic identity pivots. Soft remodeling demand and tariff uncertainty pressure BSET, HOFT, and FGI, while FLXS and VIRC navigate choppy volumes with discipline. The most distinctive stories involve business-model transformations: ATER abandons consumer products for mineral trading and AI exploration, EFOI shifts from LED lighting to data-center energy storage, and XMAX layers an AI subsidiary and a SpaceX-linked investment onto legacy furniture. MWYN’s own AI-infrastructure pivot brings volatile trading but firm analyst skepticism.\n\nExecution credibility separates resilient margin delivery at COOK, LCUT, and LOVE from distress at SNBR, where liquidity is tight, guidance absent, and governance under strain, and from PRPL, where early wholesale traction sits beneath penny-stock debt fears. AMWD’s pending MasterBrand acquisition adds scale potential alongside integration risk, while KEQU works through acquisition integration as international momentum provides a partial offset. The batch challenges readers to weigh steady cycle management against bets on unproven futures.",
  "summary_date": "2026-06-14"
